+# Re-archive transcript merge implementation plan
+
+Status: implementation applied; active and untracked because the full completion gate is blocked by the supplied linked dependency setup. Final independent patch review found no remaining actionable patch issues.
+
+Goal: preserve archive-only messages when a trimmed native or replay revival is re-archived, without mixing unrelated runtime generations.
+
+Scope: HistoryManager archive assembly, a focused transcript merge helper, and regression tests. Work in this checkout; do not commit or create branches/worktrees.
+
+- [x] Reproduce archive-only history loss using the real gzipped history writer.
+- [x] Merge verified prior same-thread/provider data for continuity revivals, including replay into a new provider session; retain session replacement for unrelated runtime inputs.
+- [x] Require persisted/index source generation agreement and tolerate missing, corrupt, or malformed prior data.
+- [x] Prefer current copies by id or renumbering-independent fingerprint; match copies one-for-one and preserve parallel tool identities and repeated occurrences.
+- [x] Run focused tests and all canonical verification commands; record failures accurately below.
+- [x] Obtain a fresh independent patch review and resolve every actionable patch finding.
+- [ ] Obtain independent completion-gate PASS. Final review has no actionable patch findings, but the linked-install failure prevents a fully passing Gate 0.
+- [ ] Close this document only after the required completion gate passes.
+
+## As-built
+
+`history-archive-merge.ts` reuses verified history coverage and its already-loaded conversation before merging. `HistoryManager.archiveInstance()` derives persisted messages, counts, previews, and snippets from that merged transcript. Coverage decisions still use the current runtime transcript.
+
+Continuity revival explicitly carries `metadata.continuityRevival === true`, allowing native and replay restoration to retain their logical thread despite a changed provider session. Other provider sessions replace the old transcript. A file whose original runtime id or session disagrees with its index is always excluded. Missing legacy session ids are normalized defensively.
+
+Fingerprints include exact type, timestamp, and content; tools additionally retain call identity and call input. Inferred tool-result names do not change identity. Only identity-bearing fields are projected, so malformed legacy thinking cannot abort archival. Matching reserves stable ids first, then consumes renumbered copies one-for-one. The final union is stably sorted by timestamp without mutating either input.
+
+## Verification after the last code change
+
+- Focused: **5 files, 84 tests passed** (`_scratch/test-run.pid-92533.log`).
+- Passed under Node 24.15.0 from `.nvmrc`: `npx tsc --noEmit`, `npm run typecheck:spec`, `npm run lint`, `npm run check:ts-max-loc`, `npm run build:main`, `npm run build:renderer`.
+- Full suite, four workers: **29,996 passed, 7 skipped, 1 failed / 30,004**. Evidence: `_scratch/test-run.rearchive-verified.log`, `_scratch/test-results.rearchive-verified.json`.
+- Sole full-suite failure: `scripts/__tests__/dependency-compatibility.spec.ts` / `keeps the installed production tree valid`. The supplied linked dependency tree belongs to a checkout whose `package.json` and `package-lock.json` differ from this workspace. Manifests, dependencies, and test harness were left untouched.
+- An earlier full run also hit the Codex native meaningful-stop test. That entire spec passed 7/7 in isolation and in the latest full run; no adapter or adapter-test changes were made.
+- Fresh reviews exposed replay-session, inferred-tool-name, malformed-thinking, and missing-legacy-session boundaries. Each received a regression observed failing before its fix. The missing-session reproduction is recorded in `_scratch/test-run.pid-88898.log`; the earlier three are in `_scratch/test-run.pid-68937.log`.
+
+## Final independent review
+
+The third fresh verifier returned no remaining actionable patch findings, independently passed 84 focused tests plus 73 additional history/coverage/serialization tests, and passed main build, lint, and diff checks. Evidence: `_scratch/test-run.pid-98750.log` and `_scratch/test-run.pid-56366.log`. It separately reproduced the dependency failure (4 passed, 1 failed; `_scratch/test-run.pid-72275.log`) and therefore returned strict `VERDICT: FAIL` solely for the environment's Gate 0 blocker. The plan deliberately remains active and uncommitted.
